OL,4,CHuawei found guilty of stealing trade  
OL,5,Csecrets but acquitted of racketeering  
OL,6,GHuawei has been found guilty of        
OL,7,Gconspiracy to steal trade secrets and  
OL,8,Gbank fraud, but not guilty of the more 
OL,9,Gserious overarching racketeering       
OL,10,Gcharge in a landmark case in the US.   
OL,12,FIn a two-month trial, prosecutors      
OL,13,Faccused the Chinese technology and     
OL,14,Ftelecommunications giant of lying,     
OL,15,Fcheating and stealing to gain any      
OL,16,Fcompetitive advantage.                 
OL,18,FHuawei's defence team argued that      
OL,19,Fprosecutors had decided Huawei was a   
OL,20,Fcriminal organisation and built its    
OL,21,Fcase from there, but the firm's        
OL,22,Fsuccess was due to its own innovation. 
